PmWiki&#39;s [http://www.pmichaud.com/wiki/PmWiki/SpecialCharacters SpecialCharacters] page has a more nicely formatted version of this. Canadian Mind Products&#39; [http://mindprod.com/jgloss/htmlcheat.html#SPECIALCHARS HTML Cheat Sheet] has some more.

These are not strictly kosher in HTML any more. You&#39;re supposed to use
[http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/sgml/entities.html numeric codes]. Yuck.

UseMod passes through the HTML codes for special characters. These are typed with an ampersand, some text, and a semi-colon, as in the &quot;Token&quot; column in the table below.

